{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes safe, coverage-oriented exploration: move forward or random_walk when clear, recover with backward or directed turn when blocked, and use full_rotate only as a last-resort scan after repeated failures. Each obstacle event leads to a dedicated recovery state with a single safe controllable. The design avoids oscillations, ensures progress, and always returns to forward exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration, with deterministic transitions and single controllable per state."
  ],
